---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site collects: no cookies, no accounts, no tracking scripts that identify you."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <div class="wrap narrow prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} />
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies. There is no login, no account, no newsletter and no comment
      system, so there is nothing to remember about you between visits. That is also why you are
      not seeing a consent banner: there is nothing to consent to.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    {site.cloudflareAnalyticsToken ? (
      <p>
        We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookie-free and does not fingerprint visitors.
        It records aggregate page views, referrers and country. It cannot identify you and we
        cannot see individual visitors.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        No analytics are currently running. If that changes we will use a cookie-free, non-
        fingerprinting provider and say so here.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2>Outbound links</h2>
    <p>
      Links to hosting providers may be affiliate links, which means the destination site can see
      that you arrived from here. We do not pass any information about you, because we do not have
      any. See the <a href="/disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is static and served by Cloudflare. Cloudflare processes request logs
      including IP addresses as part of delivering and protecting the site; that is standard for
      any website and is governed by Cloudflare's own privacy terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this page: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
